I had installed the all deb's on my own (and NOT by providing the link
[1] in /etc/apt/sources.list). I could not install "spgrass6".

Then I compiled/installed R 2.9.1 from source and "spgrass6" was
installable... but not rpy2.

Now I removed the "custom" R 2.9.1, copy-pasted the link [1]
in /etc/apt/sources.list and installed R via ubuntu's package manager
(that is: sudo apt-get install r-base r-base-dev. This way I could
install rpy2.

Now, it seems that I have managed to install "spgrass6" (it loads fine)
but whenever I try to load "G <- gmeta6()" in R _OR_ whenever I exit an
R session ( with q() ) I get error messages (again!!).

